<section style="background-image:url('/assets/img/hiredevelopers/her2.webp'); background-repeat:no-repeat; background-size:cover; background-position:center;">
    <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up">
        <div class="row align-items-center">
            <div class="col-lg-8 mt-5">
                <h1 class="text-white text-start pt-5 pb-3"><b>MICROSOFT DYNAMICS 365 PLUGIN DEVELOPMENT</b></h1>
                <p class="text-white pb-4">Custom CRM extensions</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-7 text-center">
            @*  <img src="~/assets/img/hiredevelopers/DevImg.png" />*@
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" style="text-align: justify;">
                <h2><b>Custom Dynamics 365 Plugin Development</b></h2>
                <p>iFOX provides Dynamics 365 plugin development services for organizations that need custom server-side development beyond standard configuration. Our Dynamics CRM plugin development approach starts with the business requirement and event context, then designs, develops, tests, and documents custom Dynamics 365 plugins that work with Dataverse and the surrounding CRM process. For broader planning, our <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/CRM%20Consulting">CRM Consulting</a> service can help define the wider solution requirements.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Requirement Analysis: Define the business rule, affected table and process, triggering event, users, data, and expected outcome before development begins.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Plugin Design: Choose the appropriate message, stage, filtering attributes, and execution mode for the required server-side behavior.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Dataverse Plugin Development: Work with Dataverse records through supported platform APIs, using efficient queries, appropriate filtering, and only the columns required by the process.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Execution Strategy: Use synchronous execution when immediate validation or processing is required, and consider asynchronous execution for work that can complete after the user-facing transaction.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Testing and Handover: Validate plugin behavior against realistic CRM scenarios, then document the solution, configuration, deployment considerations, and maintenance requirements for handover. This can support a broader <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Implementation">Dynamics 365 implementation</a>.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4 Imgborder">
                <div><img src="/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Developer working on Dynamics 365 plugin development" /></div>
                <div><img src="/assets/img/dynamics365/mod woman-equipped-computer-lab.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Woman equipped with a computer in a technology lab" /></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="call-to-action" class="call-to-action section dark-background">
    <img src="/assets/img/dynamics365/office2.webp" alt="">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row aos-init aos-animate" data-aos="zoom-in" data-aos-delay="100">
            <div class="col-xl-9 text-center text-xl-start">
                <h3>Need Dynamics 365 plugin development services?</h3>
                <p>Discuss custom server-side CRM logic with iFOX.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-xl-3 cta-btn-container text-center">
                <a class="cta-btn align-middle" href="/contact">Get Started</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-4">
                <div><img src="/assets/img/dynamics365/mod woman-equipped-computer-lab.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Woman working at a computer during plugin development" /></div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-8 Imgborder" style="text-align: justify;">
                <h2><b>Best Practices for Dynamics 365 Plugin Development</b></h2>
                <p>Reliable Microsoft Dynamics 365 plugin development balances business requirements with performance, maintainability, security, and predictable execution. iFOX reviews the plugin design and its impact on Dataverse transactions so custom server-side logic remains focused on the process it is intended to support.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Validate Input: Check incoming data, execution context, and required values before processing.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Keep Logic Focused: Design custom Dynamics 365 plugins around clear responsibilities and avoid placing unrelated process logic in one execution path. Where standard configuration is sufficient, consider <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Customization">Dynamics 365 customization</a> options first.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Consider Performance: Filter Dataverse queries, retrieve only required columns, avoid repeated processing and unnecessary API calls, and keep plug-in work appropriate to the execution mode. Related <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Power%20Platform">Power Platform</a> components should also be considered in the connected process.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Handle Exceptions: Provide clear error handling and avoid masking failures that require investigation or user guidance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Test and Maintain: Test plugin behavior against realistic CRM scenarios, review changes after platform updates, and keep technical documentation current for ongoing maintenance. Ongoing <a href="/dynamics-365-crm-services/Support">Dynamics 365 support</a> can help with future troubleshooting and review.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

